add('Low-rank computation has a measurable error,not a universal speedup','spectral/inertial-manifold projector','2025-11-18','U','Numerical linear algebra','What computational saving and approximation error follow from a genuine rank-dfactorization?',
'The recovered transformer discussion estimated enormous projection speedups from a small retained dimension. A rank factorization gives an arithmetic-count reduction for a specified linear map;whole-network speed,accuracy and energy claims require independent evidence.',
['LetW∈R^(n×n)have singular valuesσ₁≥…≥σ_n,and letW_dbe its truncatedSVD.','A rank-dfactorizationW_d=UV^Tusesn×dmatricesU,V.'],
'Optimal spectral residual and a product error bound','||W−W_d||₂=σ_(d+1). ApplyingUV^Tto a vector costs about2ndmultiply-adds instead ofn². For products with||A_j||,||B_j||≤Mand||A_j−B_j||≤ε,the difference ofL-layerlinear products is at mostLεM^(L−1).',
'Singular-value diagonalization shows the residual norm isσ_(d+1). Optimality follows because anyrank-dapproximation has a nonzero kernel vector within the span of the firstd+1right singular vectors;on that vectorWacts with norm at leastσ_(d+1). The two matrix-vector multipliesV^TxandUyuse2ndoperations to leading order. For products,insert one factor difference at a time:ΠA−ΠB=ΣA_L…A_(j+1)(A_j−B_j)B_(j−1)…B₁. Submultiplicativity bounds each term byεM^(L−1),and summing proves the estimate. Thus small per-layer error can accumulate with depth and large operator norms.',
'Taken=8192,d=16,and compare one linear application.',
'n²=67108864while2nd=262144,giving an idealized factor256for that isolated map under the same multiply-add convention. Including additional projections,attention,activations,memory movement or a different baseline changes the ratio. A formula12n/d=6144uses a different baseline workload and is not the same operation count.',
'The saving and the residual are explicit mathematical quantities;they do not imply a universal neural-network acceleration.',
'No actual retained subspace,layer residuals,hardware timing or energy benchmark was recovered. The low-rank hypothesis must be tested on the intended model and inputs.',
'Estimateσ_(d+1)and downstream Lipschitz factors for each actual layer,then compare the certified approximation error with measured latency and task accuracy.',
[('Eckart and Young, approximation by lower-rank matrices','https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02288367')])
add('A Riccati equation with a complete optimal-control proof','Riccati equation','2025-11-19','A','Optimal control','Which concrete Hamilton–Jacobi and Riccati statements can replace the unsupported viability theorem?',
'The recovered passage invokedPontryagin,HJB,Riccatiand broad system viability. A scalar linear-quadratic control problem provides a complete finite-horizon theorem with no unstated economic or geometric interpretation.',
['Letx′=u,x(0)=x₀,and minimizeJ=(1/2)∫₀ᵀ(qx²+ru²)dtwithq,r>0and no terminal cost.','SetP(t)=√(qr)tanh(√(q/r)(T−t)).'],
'Exact value and optimal feedback','The minimum isV(0,x₀)=P(0)x₀²/2,and the unique optimal control satisfiesu=−P(t)x/r. The functionPobeysP′=P²/r−qwithP(T)=0.',
'Differentiate the displayedhyperbolictangentto verify theRiccatiequation and terminal condition. For any admissible control,d(Px²/2)/dt=P′x²/2+Pxu. Add this derivative to the running cost and substituteP′=P²/r−q;the result is(r/2)(u+Px/r)². Integrating and usingP(T)=0givesJ=P(0)x₀²/2+(r/2)∫(u+Px/r)²dt. The nonnegative remainder proves the lower bound,and the feedback equation makes itzero. The feedback ODEhas a unique solution becauseP is continuous,so the optimum is attained and unique up to almost-everywhere equality. This also derives the quadraticHJBansatz rather than merely asserting it.',
'Takeq=r=1andT=1.',
'P(0)=tanh1,so the optimal cost is(tanh1)x₀²/2. The feedback weakens tozeroas t→Tbecause there is no terminal penalty. In the infinite-horizon limitP→1and the feedback tends tou=−x,the familiar stable closed loop.',
'The control theorem has exact hypotheses,an explicit solution,and a proof by completing squares.',
'This does not certify the recovered campus orAGIviability inequalities,nor aTannakiangroup. Their states,costs,constraints and uncertainty model were not specified sufficiently for a theorem.',
'For a constrained nonlinear model,derive the actualHJBorPontryaginconditions from its defined state and cost,then distinguish necessary conditions from a global sufficiency proof.',
[('Boyd, linear quadratic regulation lecture','https://stanford.edu/class/ee363/lectures/clqr.pdf')])
add('Poisson-consistent smoothing follows from commuting convolution','Poisson-consistent kernels','2025-11-18','U','Partial differential equations','When does smoothing a potential preserve its Poisson equation?',
'The recovered universal smoothing proposal connectedBarneskernels,subdivision,neural layers and gravitational potentials. A precise convolution theorem is useful and provable,but it requires regularity,translation invariance and a correctly normalized kernel.',
['OnR^dletη_εbe a smooth nonnegative mollifier of total massone.','AssumeΦandρare distributions satisfyingΔΦ=ρ,with convolutionη_ε*Φwell-defined.'],
'Poisson equation commutes with mollification','Δ(η_ε*Φ)=η_ε*ρin distributions. On a torus,a solution ofΔΦ=ρrequires meanρ=0,and smoothing preserves that compatibility condition.',
'Distributional differentiation commutes with convolution by a test function:testing againstψand integrating by parts transfersΔtoψand then toΦ,with no boundary term onR^dor the torus. ThusΔ(η_ε*Φ)=η_ε*(ΔΦ)=η_ε*ρ. Integrating a torusLaplacian giveszero,proving the necessarymeancondition. Sinceηhas massone,the mean ofη*ρequals the mean ofρ. In Fourier coordinates on a torus,the equation is−|k|²Φ̂(k)=ρ̂(k)for k≠0;both smoothed coefficients are multiplied byη̂_ε(k),so the identity is visible mode by mode. The zero potential mode remains an arbitrary additive constant.',
'Takeρ(x)=cosx on a2πperiodic circleandΦ(x)=−cosx. Use a heat mollifier with multiplier e^(−ε²k²).',
'The smoothed density ise^(−ε²)cosxand the smoothed potential is−e^(−ε²)cosx;the second derivative of the latter is exactly the former. Ifρ=1instead,there is no periodicPoissonsolution because its mean is nonzero.',
'The legitimate operator-smoothing relation is a precise PDEcommutation theorem with an exact example.',
'An arbitraryBarnesorlearnedkernelneed not have these properties,and smoothing a nonlinear operator generally does not commute with its nonlinearity. No universal computing or physical equivalence follows.',
'For a proposed kernel,prove normalization,regularity and Fourier bounds,and calculate the commutator with any variable-coefficient or nonlinear operator rather than assuming it vanishes.',
[('Hörmander, distribution theory','https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-96750-4')])
